## Confidentiality boundary

This repository deliberately contains NO supplier-specific information: no vendor
register, no assessment findings, no risk scores for named suppliers, no contract
terms, no transfer impact assessments, no audit evidence, and no list of control
gaps.

That content is classified CONFIDENTIAL and is held in private repositories. Its
absence from this repository is a control, not an omission. Contributors must not
add it. The continuous integration secret and personal-data scan enforces this
mechanically, and `jolarca-control/scripts/validate_repos.py` forbids
confidential or restricted classifications in a public repository at the
infrastructure level.

Any confidential material committed here by mistake must be treated as a security
incident under `SECURITY.md`, not merely reverted: removal from the working tree
does not remove it from history, and a force-push does not undo a clone.

## Third-party references

References to SOC 2 trust services criteria, ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A controls,
the General Data Protection Regulation, PCI DSS v4.0, the SIG Lite questionnaire
and the CSA CAIQ are to publicly available standards and frameworks. Those
standards are the property of their respective bodies — the AICPA, ISO/IEC, the
European Union, the PCI Security Standards Council, the Shared Assessments Program
and the Cloud Security Alliance — and nothing in this repository reproduces them
in full or claims any affiliation with or endorsement by them.
